{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794379373,"nonce":"owMr4sSmyVM39YjZ8NL7uofWjGc=","title":"Div::visible with a constant is not seen by incremental_update","message":"`Div::visible(v)` stores a `visible_source`. `Div::build` turns it into `display: none` when the node is created. `layout_style()` returns the raw style, and `render_props()` carries no visibility, so neither the own hash nor the taffy style update ever sees it.\n\nReproducer (blinc_layout, RenderTree): build `div().child(div().id(\"v\").w(80.0).h(30.0).visible(true))`, then `incremental_update` with the same tree built with `.visible(false)`. The result is NoChanges and the node stays shown. In the other direction, an update that does replace the node's taffy style puts back the builder's raw display, so a node built hidden can reappear.\n\nSignal-bound sources (State, Computed) are unaffected: they write the display through a property binding.\n\nDirection: expose the resolved display through `layout_style()`, or fold the constant into the hash and into the style set by `update_render_props_in_place`.","files":null}]}